      "keyInsight": "We love the fantasy of a single magic silver bullet. Swallow one blue pill, and your sunny smile returns by dinner. But curing a broken nervous system is not like fixing a flat tire. It is much more like restoring an overgrown, neglected community garden. You need fertilizer, good soil, steady rain, weed pulling, and constant patience. Medication is the chemical fertilizer that balances acidic dirt in the dark. Talk therapy is the wooden trellis that guides growing vines upward. Daily habits like walking and regular sleep are the garden fence keeping foxes away. The grand secret is that no single tool can do the whole job. Expecting pills alone to heal your life is like buying fertilizer and never planting seeds.",
