      "headline": "Different Soil, Different Storms: How Background Shapes Pain",
      "keyInsight": "Depression wears different masks depending on where you stand in society. Rich people visit private clinics and discuss serotonin balance. Poor communities endure grinding stress without words for emotional collapse. In crowded tenements, chronic sorrow gets labeled as physical weariness or bad luck. Age shifts the landscape too. Teenagers lash out in anger while elderly seniors fade into silent exhaustion. Culture dictates which emotional leaks are allowed. If your culture shames tears, the body speaks through stomach ulcers and back pain. The fire is identical, but the smoke blows in different directions.",
